<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Messina year share leaps, repeats caution.</title>
<headline>Messina year share leaps, repeats caution.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     41.0	  vs 21.6</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 10.25	 vs 5.0</p>
<p>    Attrib earnings	 5.4	   vs 2.9</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   6.37	  vs 3.01</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.81	  vs 0.23</p>
<p>    Interest received     0.59	  vs 0.97</p>
<p>    Turnover		  29.86	 vs 32.88</p>
<p>Div payable October 18</p>
<p>on register October 4</p>
<p>Full name: Messina Investments Ltd</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     0.13 gain   vs  0.38 gain</p>
<p>NOTE - Messina, whose interests lie mainly in diamond and copper mining, said it expected to see an improvement in group earnings in the current year.</p>
<p>The firm also advised shareholders to continue to be cautious when dealing its shares as the group is still in talks which, if concluded, may effect the value of the group's stock. -- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
